From: =?UTF-8?q?Ond=C5=99ej=20Jirman?= <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 14 Nov 2021 01:14:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/90] usb: typec: fusb302: Add OF extcon support

Look the extcon provider up by phandle, so a device tree can point at the
USB2 PHY that runs BC1.2 charger detection. Until now it could only be
named through linux,extcon-name, which probe reserves for ACPI platforms,
leaving a DT board on a dedicated charger stuck on whatever the Type-C
resistors advertise.

Resolve it on first use rather than in probe, because the provider can sit
behind a driver that waits on this one and resolving it during probe would
close that cycle.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/fusb302.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/fusb302.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/fusb302.c
index 69f2bacec4da..9c46d1e53e98 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/fusb302.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/fusb302.c
@@ -443,6 +443,16 @@ static int tcpm_get_current_limit(struct tcpc_dev *dev)
 	int current_limit = 0;
 	unsigned long timeout;
 
+	/*
+	 * To avoid cycles in OF dependencies, we get extcon when necessary
+	 * outside of probe function.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_present(chip->dev->of_node, "extcon") && !chip->extcon) {
+		chip->extcon = extcon_get_edev_by_phandle(chip->dev, 0);
+		if (IS_ERR(chip->extcon))
+			chip->extcon = NULL;
+	}
+
 	if (!chip->extcon)
 		return 0;
 
